iommu/amd: Clear PerfOpt before disabling the IOMMU

amd_iommu_perfopt_set() reads MMIO_EXT_FEATURES to check whether the
IOMMU supports PerfOpt. The suspend path calls it from iommu_disable()
after CONTROL_IOMMU_EN has already been cleared, so the feature check
now performs an MMIO access against a disabled IOMMU.

Move the PerfOpt clear before the IOMMU disable sequence so the check
and the register write happen while the IOMMU is still accessible.
The activation state is still preserved for resume.

Fixes: b32ecac779bb ("iommu/amd: Enable PerfOpt automatically for integrated GPUs")
--- a/drivers/iommu/amd/init.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/amd/init.c
@@ -470,6 +470,13 @@
 	if (!iommu->mmio_base)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Clear PerfOpt before disabling the IOMMU. amd_iommu_perfopt_set()
+	 * reads MMIO_EXT_FEATURES, so the IOMMU must still be enabled.
+	 */
+	amd_iommu_perfopt_set(iommu, false);
+	iommu->perfopt_enabled = perfopt_enabled;
+
 	/* Disable command buffer */
 	iommu_feature_disable(iommu, CONTROL_CMDBUF_EN);
 
@@ -490,10 +497,6 @@
 
 	/* Clear IRTE cache disabling bit */
 	iommu_feature_disable(iommu, CONTROL_IRTCACHEDIS);
-
-	/* Clear hardware while preserving the activation state for resume. */
-	amd_iommu_perfopt_set(iommu, false);
-	iommu->perfopt_enabled = perfopt_enabled;
 }
 
